return runs.run('history-bounds-writer', {agent:'worker', task:'You are the sole repository writer. Fix production loss of large session history using strict red-green TDD. Do not commit, push, deploy, modify `.pi-subagents/`, alter any database schema or index, or change WAL, encryption, backup, restore, or storage layout. Production facts: one session has 36 messages. Legacy `/api/sessions/{id}/messages` serializes to 1,372,260 bytes, above `WorkerHttpDispatcher` limit 1,048,576. The managed frontend serializes all `session.read` calls on one encrypted connection. Oversized history closes that connection, so queued session metadata never reaches runner. Rows remain intact, but browser reports failed metadata and disables send. Keep legacy messages endpoint unchanged for compatibility.

Add bounded APIs: `GET /api/sessions/{session_id}/messages/page` returns deterministic metadata ordered by `(created_at,id)` without `content` or `full_message`, with null-versus-empty field state, exact character lengths, and a strictly validated compact cursor. Use a fixed bounded page and parameterized keyset SQL. `GET /api/sessions/{session_id}/messages/{message_id}/field?name=content|full_message&offset=N` returns a server-sized string chunk, current offset, and strictly advancing next offset or null. Choose at most 32,768 characters so worst-case JSON escaping stays safely below 1 MiB. Cross-session IDs and invalid fields must fail closed. Use `run_db_operation_for_request` so encrypted opens stay off the event loop. Keep every response bounded. Extend backend runner RPC and frontend runtime transport exact allowlists with `session.read`; reject near matches.

Switch Session history loading to these endpoints. Reconstruct exact current Message shape, Unicode, null, empty strings, order, timestamps, roles, turn fields, and structured assistant blocks. Detect repeated cursors, repeated or decreasing offsets, offset beyond advertised length, early termination, length mismatch, and excessive requests. Preserve cancellation when navigating sessions. History errors must not overwrite a successful metadata result, and metadata errors must not erase successfully loaded history. Add backend route, authorization, worker-size, and large-history tests. Add frontend runtime transport and Session tests, including total history above 1 MiB and one multi-chunk structured message. Run focused red-green cycles, full backend and frontend tests, TypeScript checks, production build, Black, isort, flake8, mypy, and diff checks. Report exact files and remaining risks.', context:'fork', turnBudget:{maxTurns:65,graceTurns:5}, toolBudget:{soft:200,hard:290,block:['read','grep','find','ls']}});

