input.workflowScript:
const task = [
'In /Users/user/projects/yinshi, remove remaining cold-start latency so the deployed session reaches under 2 seconds. You are sole writer. Do not commit or touch .pi-subagents/. Strict red-green TDD.',
'Production measurements: direct managed bundle plus active discovery in a warm realm takes 1.50 seconds. Gzip decode is 34 ms. A fresh iframe reaches conversation readiness in 3.1-3.9 seconds. Cold Noise WASM initialization and the separate active connection dominate.',
'1. Add active_run_id to every history bundle envelope. Inside the existing bundle read transaction, query prompt_runs for this session with status in starting, running, stopping. Return one 32-hex ID or null. Require the same value on every page. Frontend validates it and exposes it through a new optional SessionHistoryLoadOptions callback named onBundledActiveRun. Invoke the callback only after the full bundle snapshot succeeds. Legacy and 413 fallback must not invoke it. Add exact backend, model, frontend, compression-bound, active/null, and multipage-invariance tests.',
'2. In Session.tsx, when managed historyBundleSupported is true and DecompressionStream exists, do not start initial active discovery. Load the bundle and capture active_run_id through the callback. Bootstrap history using that ID and skip second discovery when callback ran. This must preserve assistant deduplication. Bootstrap immediately, which lets live event attachment start after conversation display. If bundle is unavailable and legacy fallback runs, perform active discovery after history before bootstrap. For non-bundle runtimes, retain current concurrent discovery/history behavior and second discovery. Add public tests proving bundle-capable sessions issue no /runs/active request before history bootstrap, attach the bundled active ID, deduplicate its assistant row, and legacy fallback still discovers active state.',
'3. Export preloadEncryptedRunnerCrypto from encryptedRunnerClient. It must start the existing cached Noise module initialization without creating keys or connections. In frontend main startup, call it immediately only for /app paths. Swallow preload rejection so the real connection reports its normal error later. Add tests proving preload shares the same module promise with later connections, creates no capability or WebSocket, and main startup does not produce unhandled rejection.',
'Preserve feature advertisement, exact scope authorization, active-run recovery behavior, cancellation, BYOC/local/hosted legacy behavior, secret handling, and all limits. Run focused red-green tests, full frontend and backend tests where backend changes, all static checks, typecheck, changed-file Prettier, build, and diff check. Report residual risks.'
].join('\n');
return runs.run('bundle-active-preload', {agent:'worker', task, cwd:'/Users/user/projects/yinshi', context:'fork'});

